{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VGVo7YyDtvPCv3ribtwNse","type":"tool_result","content":"14efc768 chore(pose): bind the vread matrix to its review\n3e2bdbc6 chore(pose): index the vread matrix\nd9bad9ff chore(pose): record the vread matrix\n5e606ae7 chore(pose): index the vread round r4 fixes\nef1bf6ae fix(pose): read the index within its bound through one open file\n73bedc4b chore(pose): record review round 3 of the validate-reads spec\ne9809452 chore(pose): index the vread binding\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\nindex 2b3f7198..b45ef22f 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\n@@ -114,6 +114,7 @@ Each requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n - 2026-11-26: `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` in `gitCommandContext`; the work-tree diffs of the ready-transition read, scope selection, `report --since` and the review history ledger read `git status` (`WorktreeChanges`, `WorktreeChangedNames`). `TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone`, `TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex` and `TestWorktreeReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone` fail with each guard mutated out (the optional-locks setting, each caller's `git diff` restored, the content comparison); the last also checks the answers equal `git diff` for a commit since the base, a modified, a deleted and a staged-new file. A first private-index version was refused by the full suite (D1).\n - 2026-11-26: review round 1 (rrn-b249b5d958a5d8ff) requested changes with N1–N9: the status-based answers differed from `git diff` for a submodule ignored by `.gitmodules`, a submodule with uncommitted content, symlinks and a directory replaced by a file, unmerged entries, a POSE root below the repository top, intent-to-add, staged-then-reverted changes and a range base. They were withdrawn: the callers run their original `git diff` again, reading the index through a `memfd` (D1). `TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff` builds those states and requires each read to answer byte for byte as the plain diff, leave `.git/index` identical and leave no lock; it also runs the review history ledger's diff (N9). Each guard fails its test mutated out.\n - 2026-11-26: review round 2 (rrn-233e9d0e27a7230a) requested changes. N10: the memfd carried a new time, so a racily clean entry was trusted on its stat and a real change was hidden; the memfd (and the copy outside Linux) now keeps the index's modification time, and `TestReadOnlyIndexDiffSeesARacilyCleanEntry` fails with the current time in its place. N11: without an index file the read runs plainly instead of failing, and `check` applies the read-only index to its diff only (`TestValidationReadsAnswerWithoutAnIndex` fails with the missing-index case removed; the diff-only restriction is behaviour-preserving, as `ls-files` never writes, and has no test of its own). N13: scope selection keeps the cause of a failed read, and the index read reports its own error. N12 is a follow-up.\n+- 2026-11-26: review round 3 requested changes with follow-ups only (N14–N17), because its sandbox rerun of `validate` failed for environment reasons and was recorded `failed`. N17: the index is checked and read through one open file within the bound. N14–N16 are follow-ups.\n \n ### Results summary\n The full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n@@ -141,4 +142,6 @@ The engine's Git reads during `validate`, `check` and `report` no longer rewrite\n L1 and L2 above.\n \n ### Follow-ups\n-- [open] Keep a split-index read from touching the modification time of `.git/sharedindex.<hash>`, which Git updates when it reads the shared index (review round 2, N12). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\n+- [open] Keep a split-index read from touching the modification time of `.git/sharedindex.<hash>`, which Git updates when it reads the shared index (review rounds 2 N12, 3 N15). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\n+- [open] Report a failed index read in the ready-transition check instead of dropping its diff, and bound the index location lookup by the caller's deadline (review round 3, N14). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\n+- [open] Add unmerged, range-base and dirty-submodule cases to the read-only diff equivalence test, and run the review history reader in the CLI concurrency test (review round 3, N16). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\nindex ac39ecd0..f277a7c3 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@ package pose\n \n import (\n \t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"io\"\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"os/exec\"\n \t\"strings\"\n@@ -28,22 +29,29 @@ func ReadOnlyIndex(cmd *exec.Cmd, root string) (func(), error) {\n \t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be located: %w\", root, err)\n \t}\n \tpath := strings.TrimSuffix(string(out), \"\\n\")\n-\tinfo, err := os.Lstat(path)\n-\tif os.IsNotExist(err) {\n+\tif _, err := os.Lstat(path); os.IsNotExist(err) {\n \t\t// No index yet: there is no stat cache to refresh, so the plain read\n \t\t// writes nothing (review round 2, N11).\n \t\treturn func() {}, nil\n \t}\n+\t// One open file is checked and read, within the bound (review round 3,\n+\t// N17): a file swapped in between cannot escape it.\n+\tf, err := os.Open(path)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be read: %w\", root, err)\n \t}\n-\tif !info.Mode().IsRegular() || info.Size() > diffIndexLimit {\n-\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s is not a regular file within %d bytes\", root, diffIndexLimit)\n+\tdefer f.Close()\n+\tinfo, err := f.Stat()\n+\tif err != nil || !info.Mode().IsRegular() {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s is not a regular file\", root)\n \t}\n-\traw, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n+\traw, err := io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(f, diffIndexLimit+1))\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be read: %w\", root, err)\n \t}\n+\tif len(raw) > diffIndexLimit {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s is larger than %d bytes\", root, diffIndexLimit)\n+\t}\n \t// The copy keeps the index's modification time: Git trusts an entry on\n \t// its stat only when the file is older than the index, so a fresher copy\n \t// would hide a change made in the index's own second (review round 2,\n/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3fa02db07a/claude-review/tmp/claude-1000\n/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3fa02db07a/claude-review/tmp\n/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-ready","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"51097c80-b5c4-4f9f-a49f-0bea1bc1d5e6","timestamp":"2026-11-26T18:42:35.537Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"14efc768 chore(pose): bind the vread matrix to its review\n3e2bdbc6 chore(pose): index the vread matrix\nd9bad9ff chore(pose): record the vread matrix\n5e606ae7 chore(pose): index the vread round r4 fixes\nef1bf6ae fix(pose): read the index within its bound through one open file\n73bedc4b chore(pose): record review round 3 of the validate-reads spec\ne9809452 chore(pose): index the vread binding\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\nindex 2b3f7198..b45ef22f 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\n@@ -114,6 +114,7 @@ Each requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n - 2026-