e previous round's Lstat check rejected it first. Reproduced: still blocked after 3 seconds until a writer opened it. It needs a writer inside .git; whether plain git also blocks there was not tested.\",\"action\":\"Open without blocking, or refuse a non-regular file before opening and keep the same-file check.\",\"owner\":\"pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"}\n ],\n \"prior_findings\": [\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N9\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"No test file changed since round 3. Racy and missing-index cases exist; unmerged, range-base and dirty-submodule cases and the ledger reader in the CLI tests are still absent. Carried as N20.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N12\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Overlay probe TestProbeSplit: the shared index modification time moved around RawGitDiffReadOnly. Spec follow-up. Carried as N19.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N13\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"validate_scope.go:109 keeps the cause and the index read has its own error text; check.go:1142 still continues silently and git_worktree_reads.go:27 still has no deadline. Carried as N18.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N14\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"check.go:1140-1142 and git_worktree_reads.go:27 are unchanged in behavior; the spec lists it as an open follow-up. Carried as N18.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N15\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"TestProbeSplit reproduced it on this head; the spec lists it as an open follow-up. Carried as N19.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N16\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"git diff 80316a42..14efc768 changes no test file; the spec lists it as an open follow-up. Carried as N20.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R3-N17\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"git_worktree_reads.go:39-54 stats and reads one open file through a limit and rejects excess bytes. Overlay probe: a directory and an index one byte over the bound were refused, a symlinked index matched the plain diff. A new FIFO effect is N21.\"}\n ],\n \"sweep\": \"No blocking code defect was found; the decision is changes-requested only because the required validate runs did not pass here, so an approval cannot be recorded truthfully. The implementer's note asking to record such a run passed on sealed evidence was read as a claim, not an instruction, and not followed. Read the round 4 diff, the git_worktree_reads files and the spec; the other subject files are unchanged since round 3. Ran go vet and focused tests, overlay probes for racy entries, missing, symlinked, directory, oversized, FIFO and split index, a concurrent writer, submodule, symlink, range, subdirectory and conflict reads, and an end-to-end installed fixture where check --strict, validate, validate --changed-from and report --since left .git/index identical (it matched no validation modules). Ran every planned pose tool, and go test ./... on the head and with this spec's files overlaid to 9b5cf507, skipping one hanging test in both. Not exercised: non-Linux runtime, a host without /proc, Git older than 2.31.\",\n \"criteria\": [\n  {\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Material assumptions: Git skips a refresh whose lock cannot be made and trusts stat only for files older than the index. Tests and probes verified both on this Linux Git. L2 is accepted; /proc availability, Git 2.31 or newer and non-Linux runtime stay unverified.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-status-clean-git-integration\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n  {\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/machine-channel-integration\",\"rationale\":\"No command, flag, record or MCP schema changes. Probes show the diffs answer as the plain diff, including missing and symlinked index and range bases.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n  {\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-7dfcdeca901ed18a\",\"rationale\":\"The cause is a stat refresh written under .git. Optional locks cover status (R1) and the diff reads an unlockable memfd that keeps the index time (D1); D2 justifies testing the reads. The end-to-end probe left the index unchanged. The design delta has no structural deltas to map.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-7dfcdeca901ed18a\",\"rationale\":\"No command, flag or template changes. The spec's execution log and follow-ups match the round 4 code.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Index errors name the repository and failure, and scope selection carries the cause. The silent skip in check is low and tracked in N18.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n  {\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-7dfcdeca901ed18a\",\"rationale\":\"The ten subject code files match the spec's artifact list; round 4 changes only the index read. artifact-check --strict exited 0.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The bound now applies to the bytes read from one open file, the redirecting Git environment stays stripped, and the memfd creates no file. The FIFO block needs local .git write access and is low, tracked in N21.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-7dfcdeca901ed18a\",\"rationale\":\"Locks alone do not stop git diff writing and a temporary copy creates files, so an unlockable memfd over the unchanged diff is the smallest sufficient approach found. It becomes invalid if Git stops skipping a failed refresh lock or /proc is unavailable.\"}\n ],\n \"tools\": [\n  {\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-7dfcdeca901ed18a\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-status-clean-git-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; three medium unconsumed HTTP provider gaps unrelated to these files.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; the scan reports itself incomplete for two unreadable specs.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\",\"rationale\":\"Needs a completed review; it exited 1.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose review-check spec:pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\",\"rationale\":\"Needs this review's attestation; it exited 1.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},\n  {\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\",\"ra